   <refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="refbody:1;24:13">    <section class="- topic/section " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="section:1;24:26">
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="p:1;25:10">The Environmental Temperature (tempe) is the temperature of the motor’s surrounding area. There are two temperature sensors on both sides of the SMS: the temperature sensor on the outside side (not towards the motor) measures the environment temperature.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="p:2;26:10">The recorded data shows the environmental temperature scatter plot data, in the unit of Celsius (°C). The analytics system can use this data to detect the electrical or mechanical failures of the motor.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="p:3;27:10">Each record contains an array of two samples captured on the specified timestamp.</p>
      <p class="- topic/p " xtrf="file:/C:/Users/adity/Downloads/Analytics%20User%20Guide/output/sensor_information_and_specifications/tempe.dita" xtrc="p:4;28:10">For more information on API refer to the ADI OtoSense™ SMS REST API.</p>
    </section></refbody>
